  "name": "Answer WhatsApp texts, voice notes and photos with a Claude AI receptionist",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d7840615-1278-4ca2-a211-2aed7dea819b",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -512,
        96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 848,
        "content": "## Answer WhatsApp texts, voice notes and photos with a Claude AI receptionist\n\nReplies to WhatsApp text, voice notes and photos once the customer stops typing. The prompt uses a demo HVAC company.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Voice notes are transcribed by Gemini and photos described by Claude via OpenRouter. Text passes through.\n2. Each message is saved to a data table and the run waits 10 seconds.\n3. Only the run with the customer's newest message continues and merges every saved line into one.\n4. The Receptionist Agent shows typing, then answers with Claude, Postgres memory, web search and a calculator.\n5. The reply goes out as up to 3 short WhatsApp bubbles.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] WhatsApp OAuth in the trigger, WhatsApp API in Get Voice Note URL and Get Photo URL.\n- [ ] Header Auth (Bearer WhatsApp token) in both Download nodes, Mark Read and Show Typing, Send WhatsApp Reply.\n- [ ] Header Auth (Bearer OpenRouter key) in Transcribe Voice with Gemini and Describe Photo with Claude.\n- [ ] Create a data table with text columns phone and text. Select it in the three inbox nodes.\n- [ ] Anthropic, Postgres and SerpAPI credentials on the agent's sub-nodes.\n- [ ] Put your business details in the Receptionist Agent prompt, then activate and test from a real phone."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "0a98ffc9-2d79-4cf3-b332-1c70cbed596e",
